      "kind": "claim",
      "title": "Split sections form a derivation torsor with no canonical point",
      "body": "For abelian K,H, sections of K×H->H are indexed by Hom(H,K), and base-preserving shears act by translation. The action is simply transitive, so if Hom(H,K) is nontrivial no section is fixed by all shears. This lift ambiguity adds no new resonance prime but blocks canonicality.",
      "entity_id": "claim:59742530361137a27b18"
    },
    {
      "op": "entity.declare",
      "local_ref": "test",
      "kind": "test",
      "title": "Prime cyclic section-torsor controls",
      "body": "For Cp×Cp->Cp at p=2,3,5, exact enumeration gives p homomorphic sections, p shears, full section orbits, and zero common fixed sections. All assertions pass.",
